azgor wrote:
> [1]: a blank scroll (or spellbook) dipped into !oGA becomes a random
> scroll (or spellbook) (in other words, it gains an ability/effect) with
> cursedness decided by the same rule as for the magic marker --azgor

I really like this idea. Makes sense. Nowhere near as powerful as
polypiling, so not unbalancing. Also, !oGA get somewhat useless when
you've no stats to advance except Cha. And an interesting alternative
use for all those !oFH you can acquire - alcemize into !oGA and see
what you get.

> [2]: Quest leaders notice a PC's change of sex if the PC wears an
